# Secrets - never commit a Hugging Face token
.env

# MLflow run history is local, not committed.
#
# mlflow.db is a SQLite binary. GitHub push protection rejects it as a "Lob Test
# API Key": in the raw page bytes a metric name sits flush against its 32-char
# hex run id, so `test_f1` + `e70688...f42` reads as `test_<32 hex>`, which is
# exactly Lob's key format. It is a false positive, but bypassing the scanner to
# commit a regenerable binary is the wrong trade - `python -m src.train`
# rebuilds the whole store, and it is derived data either way.
mlflow.db
mlartifacts/

# Deprecated MLflow file-store layout; MLflow 3.x refuses to write to it.
mlruns/
.env.*
*.token
secrets.*

# Streamlit runtime
.streamlit/secrets.toml

# Note: data/raw/ and models/ ARE committed deliberately.
# The raw CSV (1.0 MB) keeps the analysis reproducible from a clean clone, and
# model.joblib (0.5 MB) is what the Hugging Face Space serves. Both are well
# inside git's comfortable size range, so neither needs Git LFS.
